Simple text encoder so that you get smaller file sizes.

Done a basic run length encoding, which isn't really useful for text, but has
reminded me how to use python.

Now want to do a dictionary based thing.

So scan the text and create a dictionary where each word is a key and has a
count as its data. Then cull anything with less than maybe two or three
repititions. Then create a new dictionary where the words become the data, and
there is some other key. Somehow smack this in the file with the text full of
keys. Scrap all the RLE stuff for this too I think.

Then work out how to decode it all.




Currently only works with lowercase, and also we can't have character 30 as a
key because that is the escape key. Also want some way of getting just the
right number of substitutions.
